						  RZ.name = 'RZdelete' + RZ.recordid;
						  RZ.img = '<span class="rzFaqBtn"><i class="fa fa-trash"></i><span class="sr-only">Delete</span></span>';
						  RZ.options = '';
						  if (typeof RZaction != 'undefined') RZaction('delete');
                      </script>

                      <span class="seq-no"><script language="JavaScript" type="text/JavaScript">
if (typeof RZlogin != 'undefined') RZlogin('9.00', 'revizefaq', 'u');</script>
</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <div id="collapse8150b8" class="faq-answer collapse">
                    <span data-teams="true">Anderson Geneva is the permitted party responsible for environmental cleanup.<br />Under federal environmental laws including the <a id="menure8p" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://www.epa.gov/rcra/resource-conservation-and-recovery-act-rcra-overview" rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.epa.gov/rcra/resource-conservation-and-recovery-act-rcra-overview" target="_blank" aria-label="Link Resource Conservation and Recovery Act">Resource Conservation and Recovery Act</a> (RCRA), the EPA works with state environmental regulators (Utah Department of Environmental Quality, DEQ) to regulate, permit, and oversee environmental remediation and cleanup (&ldquo;<a id="menure8r" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2020-04/documents/corrective_action_cleanup_process_timeline-rcra-508_compliant_12-20-19.pdf" rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2020-04/documents/corrective_action_cleanup_process_timeline-rcra-508_compliant_12-20-19.pdf" target="_blank" aria-label="Link corrective action">corrective action</a>&rdquo;) for sites like former steel mills that contain hazardous solid waste. In the case of the former Geneva Steel mill site, a <a id="menure8t" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://deq.utah.gov/businesses-facilities/post-closure-permit-anderson-geneva-development-inc-formerly-geneva-steel-llc" rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://deq.utah.gov/businesses-facilities/post-closure-permit-anderson-geneva-development-inc-formerly-geneva-steel-llc" target="_blank" aria-label="Link Utah Hazardous Waste Post-Closure Permit">Utah Hazardous Waste Post-Closure Permit</a> was issued to United States Steel Corporation (USS) and the purchaser of the property Anderson Geneva, LLC for post-closure care and facility-wide corrective action for dealing with the waste and debris leftover after closure of the steel mill. This is a highly regulated process which requires complex planning and approvals by the state and federal government and ongoing testing, reporting, tracking, and compliance for a myriad of clean-up activities. This permit was issued in 2004 and updated in 2010. The former mill site has been issued an EPA ID (<a id="menure8v" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://cimc.epa.gov/ords/cimc/f?p=cimc:rcra:::::p14_rcra_handler_id:utd009086133" rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://cimc.epa.gov/ords/cimc/f?p=CIMC:RCRA:::::P14_RCRA_HANDLER_ID:UTD009086133" target="_blank" aria-label="Link EPA RCRA ID: UTD009086133">EPA RCRA ID: UTD009086133</a>) and cleanup progress is closely monitored to comply with all state and federal environmental laws. Cleanup at the site is still ongoing under the permit issued to Anderson Geneva <a id="menure91" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://deq.utah.gov/businesses-facilities/gpm-enviro-project-manager#2024" rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://deq.utah.gov/businesses-facilities/gpm-enviro-project-manager#2024" target="_blank" aria-label="Link who regularly reports required information to the Utah DEQ">who regularly reports required information to the Utah DEQ</a>.</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
                
    			
