                </div>
                <script language="JavaScript" type="text/JavaScript">
if (typeof RZlistbegin != 'undefined') RZlistbegin(8)
</script>

                
                
                <!-- pageid: 46  -->
                
                <div class="faq-item">
                  <div class="faq-question">
                    <a class="faq-question-header" href="https://www.vineyardutah.gov/government/redevelopment_agency/faqs.php#collapse8152b0" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#collapse8152b0">Where Does the RDA Money Come From?</a>
                    <div class="faq-editbtns">
                      <a name="revizefaq_rz104"></a>
                      <script language="JavaScript" type="text/JavaScript">
						  RZ.module = 'revizefaq'; RZ.linkname = '';
						  RZ.template = '*none*'; RZ.recordid = '104';
						  RZ.nexturl = "editforms/revizefaq-editform.jsp";
						  RZ.popupwidth = ''; RZ.popupheight = ''; RZ.popupscroll = '';
						  RZ.img = '<span class="rzFaqBtn"><i class="fa fa-pencil"></i><span class="sr-only">Edit</span></span>';
						  RZ.set = '';
						  RZ.options = '';
						  if (typeof RZaction != 'undefined') RZaction('edititem');
                      </script>
                      <script language="JavaScript" type="text/JavaScript">
						  RZ.module = 'revizefaq';
						  RZ.recordid = '104';
						  RZ.name = 'RZdelete' + RZ.recordid;
						  RZ.img = '<span class="rzFaqBtn"><i class="fa fa-trash"></i><span class="sr-only">Delete</span></span>';
						  RZ.options = '';
						  if (typeof RZaction != 'undefined') RZaction('delete');
                      </script>

                      <span class="seq-no"><script language="JavaScript" type="text/JavaScript">
if (typeof RZlogin != 'undefined') RZlogin('1.00', 'revizefaq', 'u');</script>
</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <div id="collapse8152b0" class="faq-answer collapse">
                    <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The RDA uses a system called Tax Increment Financing (TIF),&nbsp; which reinvests future property tax revenue growth into redevelopment, not existing public budgets.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The base value of the property is frozen (in Vineyard&rsquo;s case, extremely low due to the Geneva blight). As new development raises property values, the increase (or &ldquo;increment&rdquo;) in tax revenue is reinvested into public improvements in the area.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">These funds are not new taxes &ndash; they are growth-driven dollars, which would not exist without redevelopment.<br /></span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This chart shows the model in Utah for how tax increment financing works:<br /><img src="https://www.vineyardutah.gov/Departmnts/Development/RDA/TIF Chart.png?t=202507101358250" alt="TIF Chart" /></span><span style="font-weight: 400;"><br /></span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This chart shows the actual data for Vineyard since the RDA began. As redevelopment has occurred, the taxable value of the area has increased almost 9x resulting in participating tax entities receiving quadruple the tax revenue they would have received had no redevelopment occurred:</span><iframe src="https://flo.uri.sh/visualisation/21603391/embed" title="Interactive or visual content" frameborder="0" class="flourish-embed-iframe" style="width: 100%; height: 600px;" scrolling="no" sandbox="allow-same-origin allow-forms allow-scripts allow-downloads allow-popups allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox allow-top-navigation-by-user-activation"></iframe></p>
<div style="width: 100%!; margin-top: 4px!important; text-align: right!important;"><a class="flourish-credit" style="text-decoration: none!important;" href="https://public.flourish.studio/visualisation/21603391/?utm_source=embed&amp;utm_campaign=visualisation/21603391" target="_top"><img style="width: 105px!important; height: 16px!important; border: none!important; margin: 0!important;" src="https://public.flourish.studio/resources/made_with_flourish.svg" alt="Made with Flourish" /> </a></div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                
    			
                
                <!-- pageid: 46  -->
                
                <div class="faq-item">
                  <div class="faq-question">
                    <a class="faq-question-header" href="https://www.vineyardutah.gov/government/redevelopment_agency/faqs.php#collapse8152b1" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#collapse8152b1">Does Tax Increment Financing raise your taxes?</a>
                    <div class="faq-editbtns">
                      <a name="revizefaq_rz136"></a>
                      <script language="JavaScript" type="text/JavaScript">
						  RZ.module = 'revizefaq'; RZ.linkname = '';
						  RZ.template = '*none*'; RZ.recordid = '136';
						  RZ.nexturl = "editforms/revizefaq-editform.jsp";
						  RZ.popupwidth = ''; RZ.popupheight = ''; RZ.popupscroll = '';
						  RZ.img = '<span class="rzFaqBtn"><i class="fa fa-pencil"></i><span class="sr-only">Edit</span></span>';
						  RZ.set = '';
						  RZ.options = '';
						  if (typeof RZaction != 'undefined') RZaction('edititem');
                      </script>
                      <script language="JavaScript" type="text/JavaScript">
						  RZ.module = 'revizefaq';
						  RZ.recordid = '136';
						  RZ.name = 'RZdelete' + RZ.recordid;
						  RZ.img = '<span class="rzFaqBtn"><i class="fa fa-trash"></i><span class="sr-only">Delete</span></span>';
						  RZ.options = '';
						  if (typeof RZaction != 'undefined') RZaction('delete');
                      </script>

                      <span class="seq-no"><script language="JavaScript" type="text/JavaScript">
if (typeof RZlogin != 'undefined') RZlogin('2.00', 'revizefaq', 'u');</script>
</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <div id="collapse8152b1" class="faq-answer collapse">
                    <div data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">The use of tax increment financing (TIF) in the context of community reinvestment in Utah (RDA, URA, CRA) is not designed with the intent of increasing taxes on individual property taxpayers. Rather, this financing tool re-directs the additional tax revenue from new development for a period of time to use this increased "new growth" revenue to pay for the infrastructure and costs related to redeveloping previously blighted properties. This functions as a deferral of "new growth" revenue from an earlier year to a later year in order to reinvest that new growth revenue to pay for, on a "post-performance" basis, the public costs of redevelopment (like infrastructure).<br /><br />What this means for the former Geneva steel mill industrial site and the Geneva Urban Renewal Area (Vineyard RDA) is that the vacant and blighted industrial land, after the demolition of the steel mill, is assessed a base value after the demolition. The tax revenue from that base value land continues to go to all local tax entities. The increased value of the land as redevelopment occurs produces new "incremental" tax revenue (essentially "new growth" tax revenue). This additional or incremental tax revenue is then used to pay back the costs of the infrastructure development that facilitated and made possible that increased tax value. A 75% portion of this "incremental revenue" is given to the RDA to pay for these costs after the development has occurred. A 25% share of this incremental revenue still flows to the local government taxing entities. After the increment time period (typically 25 years), all the new tax revenue then goes to the local government entities thus increasing the "new growth" at that time.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>The reason this tool is designed in this way is that it would be infeasible for a local government to pay for infrastructure to develop blighted or vacant land since that local government doesn't have significant property tax revenue from that land to fund infrastructure. In the case of Vineyard, the vacant industrial steel mill site no longer produced significant property tax revenue for the city such that the city could not raise capital or obtain bonds to build roads or utility systems that makes development possible. However, if the city could immediately finance the creation of roads and utilities, then developers could actually build homes, commercial and industrial developments which would then produce property tax revenue. Tax increment financing makes it possible to do this quickly rather than having that vacant land languish for many years.</div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                
    			
                <script language="JavaScript" type="text/JavaScript">
if (typeof RZlinktemplate != 'undefined') RZlinktemplate('revizefaq','','')
if (typeof RZ.nextseq != 'undefined') RZ.nextseq.modules['revizefaq_8']={field:'seq_no',seq:'3.00'};
</script>

            </div>
          </div>
          
          
